know it  appalls me frankly and you know I think  we just all need to say take a step back  here we're all trying to make very  difficult decisions in a complex  scenario that's far from ideal no one  wants to be this I don't want us to  leave the EU ID it's not what I voted  for it's not what I want to see happen  in fact I used to be the director of  Britain in Europe for many years so you  know that's not where I come from but we  are trying to grapple with a set of  suboptimal  options each of which are difficult  there is no easy solution here  even a second referendum which you know  I don't think there still are the votes  in Parliament that's why it wasn't put  to Parliament yesterday even on the day  of the March the vote wasn't put to  Parliament because those advocating a  second referendum know the numbers  aren't there so there's no easy path  here out of the situation that we're in  and that's why it requires compromise it  requires as all coming together and most  of all it requires us all to respect  each others opinions respect each  other's communities and each other's  situation  and respect the fact that we're all  coming at this with with the right  values and with with the future of the  country and the future of our party at  that before

